# Slice 4 · Three More Analyzers · PDF · Evaluation

*Prove the analyzer framework scales · classifier + summarizer + contract reviewer · accept PDFs · keep AI honest with an eval harness*

---

## Why

Slice-3 proved the analyzer framework with one registered class. Slice-4 proves it scales: adding three more analyzers should be *boring* — small new files, no pipeline edits. If anything stops being boring, the framework abstraction was wrong.

Three concrete UX wins land for the user this slice:
- Summaries appear on cards (slice-2 UI has the slot, currently empty)
- Urgency populates from analysis (currently null)
- Contracts get specialized review surfacing payment terms, penalties, risks

PDF support unlocks real-world testing — pilot SMEs work with PDFs, not pasted text.
The eval harness is the discipline that prevents drift as more analyzers ship: each fixture has expected output, every analyzer runs against it on every change, hallucinations stay caught.

---

## Scope

```
IN     three new analyzers
         DocumentClassifier      prompt 19.14 · applies_to=ALL · records detected_type/confidence/language/entities
                                 does NOT override user-selected Document.type yet (slice-5 enables override)
         DocumentSummarizer      prompt 19.15 · applies_to=ALL · writes summary/urgency/key_points/deadlines/obligations
         ContractReviewer        prompt 19.17 · applies_to={"contract"} · payment_terms/penalties/termination/risk

       schema additions          DocumentAnalysis gets:
                                   detected_type      VARCHAR · null
                                   confidence         FLOAT    · null
                                   language           VARCHAR · null
                                   urgency            VARCHAR · null
                                   analyzer_outputs   JSONB    · null   (full parsed output keyed by analyzer name)
                                 alembic migration · existing rows nullable

       merge extension           merge.py grows isinstance dispatch for ClassifierResult, SummaryResult, ContractResult
                                 list-shaped fields combine across analyzers (risk_flags, missing_fields)
                                 scalar fields use first-non-null wins OR analyzer-priority order
                                 analyzer_outputs[<name>] always stored full

       PDF parsing               apps/api/app/services/parsing.py · pdfplumber
                                 POST /api/documents accepts .pdf (multipart file field) OR text (existing)
                                 PDF → extract text → save raw_text on Document → analyzers run on raw_text
                                 image-only PDFs (no extractable text): status="not_supported_yet" + audit "ocr_required"

       eval harness              apps/api/tests/evals/  (new directory)
                                 fixtures from codocz §23.3 (4 fully-written demo docs · expected_extraction blocks)
                                 per-analyzer evaluation runner
                                 scoring per codocz §23.6: score 0-10 · passed bool · critical_errors · hallucinations · missing_information
                                 cli: uv run python -m app.evals.run · prints summary + writes JSON
                                 must catch the slice-3 finding: PO-reference omission in Lumina invoice

       seed extension            seed_invoices.py adds: 1 contract (contract_supplier_lumina_design) · 1 client email
                                 (email_accountant_missing_docs_april) so summarizer/classifier have variety to chew on

       frontend surfaces         /app/inbox card shows:
                                   summary text (existing slot · now populated)
                                   urgency badge (existing slot · now populated)
                                   "AI-classified as X (78%)" badge if confidence ≥ 0.6 AND
                                     detected_type differs from user-selected Document.type
                                   for type=contract: dedicated "Contract terms" panel (collapsible)

OUT    classifier overriding doc.type            slice-5
       OCR (image-only PDFs)                     slice-5
       parallel analyzer execution               later · serial is fine for slice-4
       RAG / pgvector / embeddings               slice-5
       Ask My Company live                       slice-5
       Draft Reply live                          slice-5
       multi-language UI                         post-MVP
       evaluation against real provider drift    slice-N · for now compare to expected outputs
       eval harness in CI                        slice-N · cli only for now
```

