## Acceptance

```
analyzers          three new analyzer files · each implements Protocol · each registered in registry.ANALYZERS
                   analyzers_for(supplier_invoice doc) returns [InvoiceExtractor, DocumentClassifier, DocumentSummarizer]
                   analyzers_for(contract doc)         returns [DocumentClassifier, DocumentSummarizer, ContractReviewer]

schema             alembic upgrade head adds 5 columns to document_analyses · existing rows preserved (nullable)

pipeline           upload one of the 5 existing invoices  →  3 prompt_runs (extractor + classifier + summarizer)
                   upload contract_supplier_lumina_design  →  3 prompt_runs (classifier + summarizer + contract reviewer)
                   each prompt_run records its analyzer_name + version + status

extraction         all existing slice-3 fields still extract correctly (regression check)
                   summary populates with 1-2 sentence English text
                   urgency one of low/medium/high/unknown
                   for contracts: payment_terms · penalties · termination_terms in analyzer_outputs.contract_reviewer
                   classifier records language ("ro" for the Romanian docs · "en" or "mixed" for English UI ones)

PDF                upload a text-PDF (provide one in tests/fixtures/) → text extracted → analyzers run as expected
                   image-only PDF → status="not_supported_yet" · audit event "ocr_required"

UI                 inbox card shows summary text and urgency badge (visible from listing)
                   detail panel shows full analyzer_outputs nicely (per-analyzer expandable section is fine)
                   contract docs show Contract terms panel
                   classifier disagreement badge appears only when justified

eval harness       uv run python -m app.evals.run
                   exits 0 if all fixtures pass acceptance threshold (score ≥ 7 · no critical_errors · no hallucinations)
                   exits non-zero on regressions
                   catches: invoice_lumina missing PO-reference (the slice-3 verification finding)
                   prints concise summary + writes apps/api/tests/evals/results/<timestamp>.json

honesty            no hallucinated values · ever
                   classifier "unknown" allowed when uncertain (not forced into a wrong bucket)
                   contract questions_for_human_review surfaced when LLM is unsure about a clause
```

---

## Constraints inherited

See `ops/rules.constraints.hybrid` (anchored). Slice-4 specific reinforcement:
- Every new prompt template carries inline `# prompt: <name> v1`. Do not reuse v1 across different prompts.
- Provider abstraction: still one place to import `openai`. New analyzers call `app/services/llm.py`.
- Analyzer registry: new analyzers MUST register; pipeline never special-cases.
- Eval harness must use the same prompt loader the runtime uses (no duplication of prompt text).

---

## Resolved decisions (coordinator)

```
classifier override         classifier records detected_type/confidence ONLY in slice-4
                            user-selected Document.type stays authoritative
                            UI shows disagreement badge as a soft signal · slice-5 designs override flow

multi-analyzer order        serial · order = ANALYZERS list order
                            for slice-4: classifier → summarizer → extractor (or reviewer)
                            rationale: cheap signals first; if classifier sets language="unknown" we
                            could short-circuit summarizer in future, but not yet

merge strategy              analyzer_outputs JSONB always stores full · single source of truth
                            scalar columns (summary, urgency, suggested_action) populated by merger
                              from agreed analyzer-priority order
                              summarizer wins for summary/urgency/suggested_action
                              extractor wins for fields/missing_fields/risk_flags
                              contract reviewer adds to risk_flags · adds questions_for_human_review
                            list combine semantics: dedup-by-content union (no duplicates)

PDF library                 pdfplumber · text-PDFs only · image-only PDFs flagged "ocr_required"
                            do NOT introduce a PDF.js wrapper or pypdf · one library per concern

eval scoring                per codocz §23.6 schema · 0-10 score · passed bool · separate fields for
                            critical_errors / hallucinations / missing_information / format_errors
                            pass threshold: score ≥ 7 AND len(critical_errors)==0 AND len(hallucinations)==0
                            slice-4 fixtures: 4 from §23.3 (lumina invoice + accountant email +
                            apartament email + lumina contract) · others can be added later

eval CLI runner             cli first · pytest integration deferred · keep it dependency-light
                            command: uv run python -m app.evals.run [--analyzer NAME] [--fixture NAME]

prompt versioning           all three new prompts ship as v1 · inline version line enforced
                            eval results always include prompt_version per result row

frontend                    slice-2 UI already has summary/urgency slots · just wire them
                            new: classifier disagreement badge (only when confidence ≥0.6 AND mismatch)
                            new: contract terms panel (only when type=contract AND analyzer_outputs.contract_reviewer present)

reseed required             after schema migration, drop existing 5 rows · reseed (now 7 docs)
                            5 invoices + 1 contract + 1 accountant email
```

